    {
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "channel": "stable",
      "date": "2026-09-29",
      "status": "available",
      "source": {
        "repository": "https://github.com/DreamWeave-MP/dream-ini",
        "tag": "1.0.0",
        "revision": "cd24b42bfe878e47ee9f44714e2b89517a4e848b"
      },
      "notes": {
        "summary": "First stable release: the Luau API is an l3i extension providing @dream/ini, a large import takes milliseconds instead of a fifth of a second, and the Rust and Luau APIs are under semver.",
        "migration": "Compose `dream_ini::luau::IniExtension` into the host's l3i `RuntimePlan`. A host that still wants\nthe `dreamIni` global adds `RuntimePolicy::compat_global(\"@dream/ini\", \"dreamIni\")`. Scripts that\npass numbers in multimaps must pass strings. [Embedding Luau](@/docs/luau-hosts.md) has the setup.\n",
        "added": [
          "`parseIni` accepts a Luau `buffer`, and an unknown option's error names the function and lists the known keys.",
          "Every `@dream/ini` function has a Luau type, part of the plan's generated definitions; the definitions check and the strict script build behind the test-only `luau-analysis` feature."
        ],
        "changed": [
          "Only search paths that are directories are probed, and the cfg's `data=` directories are resolved once per import: the benchmark install imports in 4.9 ms instead of 206 ms.",
          "`dataDirs` and every multimap argument are walked in place through l3i's table option reader and array visitor, one element on the stack at a time and nothing pinned, and the `game` and `encoding` options are inspected without a copy. A `dataDirs` element that is not a string is reported as `ini.importMaps.dataDirs[2]: expected a string, got number`, and a `dataDirs` that is not a table as `ini.importMaps.dataDirs: expected an array of strings, got string`.",
          "The PortMaster GUI renders through dream-soft-render without shape anti-aliasing, and skips drawing frames that did not change.",
          "Release builds use thin LTO on every platform.",
          "l3i 1.0.0 comes from crates.io."
        ],
        "fixed": [
          "An update of a cfg that sets `resources=` no longer adds a `data=` line for `resources/vfs`, one more on every import.",
          "Each INI line loses exactly one trailing carriage return, as in the C++ importer.",
          "`importMaps`, and `import_maps` in Rust, write `encoding=` as a path import does, so the Luau `encoding` option is no longer ignored."
        ],
        "breaking": [
          "The `luau` feature (`lua` still works) makes the crate an l3i extension, `luau::IniExtension`, providing the module `@dream/ini`. `lua::create_module` and `lua::register` are gone with `mlua`.",
          "Multimap values from Luau must be strings; numbers are no longer converted.",
          "Building with the `luau` feature needs l3i's toolchain: clang, lld and cross-language thin LTO.",
          "Rust 1.92."
        ]
      },
