      },
      "notes": {
        "summary": "First release: import Morrowind.ini into openmw.cfg from the command line, a desktop GUI or a handheld.",
        "added": [
          "The importer: fallback settings, `no-sound`, archives and, with `--game-files`, content files, from `--ini` into a new cfg, a copy of `--cfg`, or `--cfg` updated in place.",
          "A desktop GUI with controller navigation, opened by running `dream-ini` with no arguments.",
          "A framebuffer GUI for PortMaster handhelds, a muOS app, and a command-line build for Android.",
          "`install-launcher`, shell completions and a manual page.",
          "The importer as a Rust library, and Lua bindings through `mlua` and LuaJIT behind the `lua` feature."
        ]
      },
